a/markdown/platform-security/domain-separated-apps.md","line":30},{"title":"Domain separation and Workflow Studio","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/build-workflows/flow-designer-domain-separation.md","line":34},{"title":"Domain separation for service providers","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-security/domain-sep-landing-page.md","line":51},{"title":"Operational Technology","target":"operational-technology-overview","line":55}],"metadata":{"title":"Domain separation and Operational Technology","description":"If any conrefs are broken, re-add them from the doc/source/reuse/domain-separation/domain-separation-overview.dita file. In the short description, edit the first sentence to state whether domain separation is supported or not and add the application name. Keep the conref at the end that describes domain separation.Domain separation is supported for Operational Technology. Domain separation enables you to separate data, processes, and administrative tasks into logical groupings called domains. You can control several aspects of this separation, including which users can see and access data.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/operational-technology/manufacturing-domain-separation.html","release":"australia","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":1,"breadcrumb":["Operational Technology"],"tags":["#operational-technology","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/operational-technology/manufacturing-domain-separation.md"},
